    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. So basically you're saying the African workforce might be more prone to delays because they don't view industrial deadlines as strictly as Europeans do? If we're talking about high-precision manufacturing where even a small delay ruins a batch, does that mean those regions are inherently higher risk for quality control issues or basically just less capable of handling high-pressure, disciplined environments?",
